  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}) & =\\frac{\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x)\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)-x\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(y+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)-x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}{|}_{(0,2)} & =\\frac{2+\\operatorname{sin}\u20610-0\\operatorname{cos}\u20610}{(2+\\operatorname{sin}\u20610)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+0}{(2+0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
